<span id="9" class="anchor"></span>
<h3>


I would like to use your digital copies. What do I have to consider?
<a data-index="9" href="#9" class="pl-2 invisible">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 14.016 14" class="inline text-theme-900">
    <path d="M 11.144 0 C 10.412 0 9.679 0.286 9.107 0.828 L 7.198 2.736 C 6.402 3.531 6.179 4.709 6.53 5.696 L 7.644 4.582 C 7.676 4.232 7.835 3.914 8.09 3.659 L 9.999 1.75 C 10.317 1.432 10.73 1.273 11.144 1.273 C 11.557 1.273 11.972 1.432 12.257 1.75 C 12.861 2.354 12.861 3.372 12.257 4.008 L 10.348 5.918 C 10.094 6.172 9.776 6.331 9.425 6.364 L 8.28 7.508 C 8.598 7.573 8.916 7.636 9.235 7.636 C 9.966 7.636 10.699 7.351 11.272 6.81 L 13.181 4.901 C 14.294 3.787 14.294 1.942 13.181 0.828 C 12.608 0.286 11.876 0 11.144 0 Z  M 9.075 4.295 C 8.916 4.295 8.757 4.359 8.629 4.486 L 4.493 8.622 C 4.239 8.877 4.239 9.291 4.493 9.514 C 4.621 9.641 4.78 9.705 4.939 9.705 C 5.098 9.705 5.257 9.641 5.385 9.514 L 9.522 5.378 C 9.775 5.123 9.775 4.74 9.522 4.486 C 9.404 4.366 9.244 4.297 9.075 4.295 Z  M 4.78 6.364 C 4.048 6.364 3.316 6.649 2.743 7.19 L 0.835 9.099 C -0.278 10.213 -0.278 12.028 0.835 13.141 C 1.407 13.714 2.139 14 2.871 14 C 3.603 14 4.335 13.714 4.908 13.173 L 6.817 11.264 C 7.613 10.469 7.835 9.323 7.485 8.304 L 6.34 9.418 C 6.308 9.768 6.149 10.086 5.894 10.341 L 3.985 12.25 C 3.699 12.568 3.285 12.727 2.871 12.727 C 2.457 12.727 2.043 12.568 1.757 12.25 C 1.153 11.646 1.153 10.628 1.757 9.992 L 3.666 8.082 C 3.921 7.828 4.239 7.669 4.59 7.636 L 5.735 6.492 C 5.416 6.427 5.098 6.364 4.78 6.364 Z" />
  </svg>
</a>
</h3>

<ul class="list-disc pl-6">

<li>

<p>

Please first check the rights statement under which the digital copy you wish to use is provided. You will find this in the complete information on a digital object.

<br />

<br />

The following terms of use result from the respective rights statements:
</p>

<ol class="list-decimal pl-6">

<li>

<p>

Digital copies provided under the rights statement '

<a href="https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/deed.en" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Public Domain Mark 1.0</a>

' may be copied, modified, distributed and performed, including for commercial purposes, 

<strong>without having to ask for permission</strong>

.
</p>
</li>

<li>

<p>

For digital copies with the rights statement '

<a href="https://rightsstatements.org/page/InC/1.0/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">In Copyright</a>

', the following applies: The content may still be 

<strong>protected by copyright</strong>

. In the event of use, you are therefore responsible for clarifying and complying with copyright law.
</p>
</li>

<li>

<p>

In the case of digital copies with the rights statement '

<a href="/en/rightsstatement-vgwort">In Copyright (InC 1.0) – Rights managed by VG WORT and VG Bild-Kunst (§ 52 VGG). Use reserved for text and data mining purposes pursuant to § 44b (2) in conjunction with (3) of German Act on Copyright and Related Rights (UrhG).</a>

' 

<strong>read access and use are permitted within the scope of the applicable copyright law</strong>

. Any further use is not permitted.
</p>
</li>

<li>

<p>

Digital copies provided under the rights statement '

<a href="http://rightsstatements.org/vocab/NoC-NC/1.0/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">No copyright – non-commercial use only</a>

' were produced as part of a 

<strong>public-private partnership with Google</strong>

 and may be used for non-commercial purposes. As long as Google scans do not constitute the predominant or sole content of a publication, commercial use is also permitted. Please note our guidelines on 

<a href="/en/download-options#6">attribution</a>

 when using these digital copies.
</p>
</li>

<li>

<p>

In all other cases, please contact us (see 

<a href="/en/contact">Contact</a>

).
</p>
</li>
</ol>
</li>
</ul>

<span id="11" class="anchor"></span>
<h3>


I am interested in full texts. What possibilities are there?
<a data-index="11" href="#11" class="pl-2 invisible">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 14.016 14" class="inline text-theme-900">
    <path d="M 11.144 0 C 10.412 0 9.679 0.286 9.107 0.828 L 7.198 2.736 C 6.402 3.531 6.179 4.709 6.53 5.696 L 7.644 4.582 C 7.676 4.232 7.835 3.914 8.09 3.659 L 9.999 1.75 C 10.317 1.432 10.73 1.273 11.144 1.273 C 11.557 1.273 11.972 1.432 12.257 1.75 C 12.861 2.354 12.861 3.372 12.257 4.008 L 10.348 5.918 C 10.094 6.172 9.776 6.331 9.425 6.364 L 8.28 7.508 C 8.598 7.573 8.916 7.636 9.235 7.636 C 9.966 7.636 10.699 7.351 11.272 6.81 L 13.181 4.901 C 14.294 3.787 14.294 1.942 13.181 0.828 C 12.608 0.286 11.876 0 11.144 0 Z  M 9.075 4.295 C 8.916 4.295 8.757 4.359 8.629 4.486 L 4.493 8.622 C 4.239 8.877 4.239 9.291 4.493 9.514 C 4.621 9.641 4.78 9.705 4.939 9.705 C 5.098 9.705 5.257 9.641 5.385 9.514 L 9.522 5.378 C 9.775 5.123 9.775 4.74 9.522 4.486 C 9.404 4.366 9.244 4.297 9.075 4.295 Z  M 4.78 6.364 C 4.048 6.364 3.316 6.649 2.743 7.19 L 0.835 9.099 C -0.278 10.213 -0.278 12.028 0.835 13.141 C 1.407 13.714 2.139 14 2.871 14 C 3.603 14 4.335 13.714 4.908 13.173 L 6.817 11.264 C 7.613 10.469 7.835 9.323 7.485 8.304 L 6.34 9.418 C 6.308 9.768 6.149 10.086 5.894 10.341 L 3.985 12.25 C 3.699 12.568 3.285 12.727 2.871 12.727 C 2.457 12.727 2.043 12.568 1.757 12.25 C 1.153 11.646 1.153 10.628 1.757 9.992 L 3.666 8.082 C 3.921 7.828 4.239 7.669 4.59 7.636 L 5.735 6.492 C 5.416 6.427 5.098 6.364 4.78 6.364 Z" />
  </svg>
</a>
</h3>

<ul class="list-disc pl-6">

<li>

<p>

Full texts (OCR = Optical Character Recognition) are available for the majority of the digital copies. These were generated automatically. The resulting machine-searchable texts have not been intellectually reworked. Depending on the quality of the original, this may result in errors or deviations from the original text in some cases. 
</p>

<p>

The hit list can be restricted to 'Full text' via the 'Supported features' facet. Full-text indexed digital copies can be searched in the viewer (see 

<a href="/en/viewer-help#16">Meta data, tocs and search within object</a>

). In addition, the extracted text can be placed directly over the image (see 

<a href="/en/viewer-help#20">Image tool bar und text overlay options</a>

).
</p>

<p>

Please also note our 

<a href="/en/download-options">download options</a>

 and the information on our 

<a href="/en/interfaces">interfaces</a>

.
</p>
</li>
</ul>

<span id="13" class="anchor"></span>
<h3>


Which picture credits do I have to add when using an image?
<a data-index="13" href="#13" class="pl-2 invisible">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 14.016 14" class="inline text-theme-900">
    <path d="M 11.144 0 C 10.412 0 9.679 0.286 9.107 0.828 L 7.198 2.736 C 6.402 3.531 6.179 4.709 6.53 5.696 L 7.644 4.582 C 7.676 4.232 7.835 3.914 8.09 3.659 L 9.999 1.75 C 10.317 1.432 10.73 1.273 11.144 1.273 C 11.557 1.273 11.972 1.432 12.257 1.75 C 12.861 2.354 12.861 3.372 12.257 4.008 L 10.348 5.918 C 10.094 6.172 9.776 6.331 9.425 6.364 L 8.28 7.508 C 8.598 7.573 8.916 7.636 9.235 7.636 C 9.966 7.636 10.699 7.351 11.272 6.81 L 13.181 4.901 C 14.294 3.787 14.294 1.942 13.181 0.828 C 12.608 0.286 11.876 0 11.144 0 Z  M 9.075 4.295 C 8.916 4.295 8.757 4.359 8.629 4.486 L 4.493 8.622 C 4.239 8.877 4.239 9.291 4.493 9.514 C 4.621 9.641 4.78 9.705 4.939 9.705 C 5.098 9.705 5.257 9.641 5.385 9.514 L 9.522 5.378 C 9.775 5.123 9.775 4.74 9.522 4.486 C 9.404 4.366 9.244 4.297 9.075 4.295 Z  M 4.78 6.364 C 4.048 6.364 3.316 6.649 2.743 7.19 L 0.835 9.099 C -0.278 10.213 -0.278 12.028 0.835 13.141 C 1.407 13.714 2.139 14 2.871 14 C 3.603 14 4.335 13.714 4.908 13.173 L 6.817 11.264 C 7.613 10.469 7.835 9.323 7.485 8.304 L 6.34 9.418 C 6.308 9.768 6.149 10.086 5.894 10.341 L 3.985 12.25 C 3.699 12.568 3.285 12.727 2.871 12.727 C 2.457 12.727 2.043 12.568 1.757 12.25 C 1.153 11.646 1.153 10.628 1.757 9.992 L 3.666 8.082 C 3.921 7.828 4.239 7.669 4.59 7.636 L 5.735 6.492 C 5.416 6.427 5.098 6.364 4.78 6.364 Z" />
  </svg>
</a>
</h3>

<ul class="list-disc pl-6">

<li>

<p>

Please state:
</p>

<ul class="list-disc pl-6">

<li>

<p>

The holding library has to be indicated in any case, if this is not the Bavarian State Library the holding library is mentioned next to the 'call number' 
</p>
</li>

<li>

<p>

Call number
</p>
</li>

<li>

<p>

Page or folio number of the image you use
</p>
</li>

<li>

<p>

URN of the digitized object
</p>
</li>

<li>

<p>

Only for Rights Statement NoC-NC (No copyright – non-commercial use only): 'digitized by Google'
</p>
</li>
</ul>

<p>

You will find the correct call number and URN on the website of the digitized object or in the BSB-Catalogue (OPACplus).
</p>

<p>

For example:
</p>

<ul class="list-disc pl-6">

<li>

<p>

Bayerische Staatsbibliothek München, ESlg/4 Zool. 382-2, p. 11, urn:nbn:de:bvb:12-bsb00068689-9
</p>
</li>

<li>

<p>

Staatliche Bibliothek Regensburg, 999/2Theol.syst.151, fol. 6v, urn:nbn:de:bvb:12-bsb11059739-6, digitized by Google
</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>

